{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. I checked the second-floor printer (BL-PR-FL2) and it really is offline. It isn't reaching the network at all, so the problem is the printer, not your computer. It stopped checking in this morning and isn't reporting any error to us. Could you or someone near it try these steps? 1) Look at the printer's screen for any error, like a paper jam, no paper or toner, or an open door, and clear it. 2) Turn the printer off, wait 30 seconds, and turn it back on. 3) Check that the network cable on the back is plugged in firmly and that the small light next to it is on. Then please reply to tell me what the screen showed and whether it came back. If it's still offline after the restart, I'll pass it to our next-level team to look for a network or hardware fault. In the meantime, the first-floor printer (BL-PR-FL1) is online. To use it, go to Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Printers & scanners > Add device. If it isn't listed, choose \"Add manually\" and type BL-PR-FL1.",
  "internal_note": "Sender: James O'Connor (user_id 8, Operations, active account, device BL-DT-0108). I ran the KB-022 quick check: BL-PR-FL2 shows online=false, last_checkin 2026-10-09T10:10:49Z, no warnings. That means the printer itself is down, not the user's machine, so KB-023 doesn't apply. Alternate printer BL-PR-FL1 is online (checked in 15:04:49Z), and I gave the user the KB-024 steps to add it. I asked the user to check the printer screen for errors, power cycle it for 30 seconds, and check the network cable and link light. Next step: if it is still offline after the power cycle with no error shown, escalate to Tier 2 as a possible network or hardware fault, per KB-022. Re-run check_device_status on BL-PR-FL2 after the user replies.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-022",
    "KB-024"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
